// UNCONFIGURED -- this case produces no particle shrinkage as it stands.
//
// On showcase/poster-demo the shrink rate came from an inline Ychar branch in
// lambdaDotModel::update(). That branch is not on main: PR #43 replaced it
// with a selectable model, chosen by `lambdaMode` here. With no lambdaMode
// key, LambdaDotCalculationModel::New falls back to `constant`, and
// constantLambdaDot then reads `lambdaValue` with a default of 0.0 -- so
// lambdaDot is identically zero and the particles never shrink. The fallback
// is silent; nothing in the log says the case is misconfigured.
//
// The equivalent of the old Ychar branch is
//
//     lambdaMode        exactDifferential;
//     dlambdaOverDYmi   { char <m^4/kg>; wood <m^4/kg>; }
//
// but the coefficients are a physical choice this case has never made. Left
// unset deliberately, pending that decision -- see the rebase plan.

lambdaDot       constant 1.0;   // dead entry, read by nothing on main

